4.1. Required character name
As a condition of the permissions in this license, preserve the character's
official names: "타이리" in Korean and "Tyri" in English. Do not rename the
character, substitute another character name, or present the character as a
differently named character. This requirement applies to original Materials
and modified or adapted versions, including redistributed versions.
Where the character is named in an interface, publication, demonstration or
other presentation, use the official name appropriate to that language.
Include both official names as "타이리 (Tyri)" in the accompanying credits,
README, documentation or about screen, together with the attribution required
by Section 4. If none of these accompanies the use, include that credit in
the presentation itself. A permanently visible name label on every animation
frame is not required. A separate application or project may have its own
name, provided the character itself remains identified as 타이리 / Tyri.

